<b>What is it?</b>

22:21.190 --> 22:22.590
<b>What is that?</b>

22:38.140 --> 22:39.300
<b>It vanished...</b>

22:52.250 --> 22:59.820
Daremo shiranai kotoba de kimi he to

22:52.250 --> 22:59.820
On that nostalgic hill, I sang out to you

22:59.820 --> 23:06.530
Utaikaketa natsukashii oka de

22:59.820 --> 23:06.530
words that no one else knew.

23:09.530 --> 23:17.030
Tomare soyokaze kawaranu omoide

23:09.530 --> 23:17.030
The dying breeze and my unchanged memories

23:17.030 --> 23:23.710
Sotto misete ano koro no boku wa

23:17.030 --> 23:23.710
gently reveal to me what I was like back then.

23:23.710 --> 23:31.150
Aa yume wo aishite hitori ni natta

23:23.710 --> 23:31.150
Ah, I thought that being alone

23:31.150 --> 23:35.950
Sore de ii to omotta

23:31.150 --> 23:35.950
and cherishing my dream would be fine.

23:35.950 --> 23:44.630
Haruka na sora ni wa ima mo kimi ga iru darou

23:35.950 --> 23:44.630
I wonder if you’re still there right now in the distant sky?

23:44.630 --> 23:53.230
Yasashiku ikiru yo afureru namida koraeta

23:44.630 --> 23:53.230
Now I lead a simple life, having suppressed my overflowing tears.

23:53.230 --> 24:02.010
Mirai no melody ga shizuka ni yureru kisetsu

23:53.230 --> 24:02.010
The melody of the future is in the quietly stirring seasons.

24:02.010 --> 24:10.720
Aitai na itsu no hi ka... mattete

24:02.010 --> 24:10.720
I want to see you again, and I’m waiting for that day.

24:10.720 --> 24:19.260
Aitai ne boku wa mada humming boy

24:10.720 --> 24:19.260
I want to see you again, but I’m still a humming boy.

24:19.970 --> 24:22.040
<b>Rokkun, Rokkun, we’ve got trouble!</b>

24:19.970 --> 24:22.980
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

24:22.040 --> 24:22.440
<b>What’s wrong?</b>

24:22.440 --> 24:25.140
<b>Grandma left this letter and went off somewhere!</b>

24:25.140 --> 24:26.180
<b>What?</b>

24:26.180 --> 24:28.350
<b>“Chase me to Yokohama,
Blue light Yokohama...”</b>

24:28.350 --> 24:30.850
<b>“...Yokohama Next to the Ports,
Twilight Yokohama...”</b>

24:30.850 --> 24:32.750
<b>Where could she have gone?</b>

24:32.750 --> 24:33.950
<b>Weren’t you listening to me?</b>

24:33.950 --> 24:35.320
<b>She’s in Yokohama. <i>Yokohama</i>.</b>

24:35.320 --> 24:37.120
<b>What prefecture is that in?</b>

24:37.120 --> 24:39.560
<b>You’re a doofus. It’s in the Yokohama
Prefecture, obviously!</b>

24:39.560 --> 24:41.590
<b>Yokohama Prefecture, huh?
That sure sounds nice!</b>

24:41.590 --> 24:44.060
<b>I wonder why she didn’t take me along with her?</b>

24:44.060 --> 24:46.100
<b>Okay! Why don’t we go there, too?</b>

24:46.100 --> 24:47.130
<b>Isn’t it far away?</b>

24:47.130 --> 24:49.530
<b>Nope! I think we can get there in about an hour.</b>

24:49.530 --> 24:50.630
<b>Well then, we’re off!</b>

24:50.640 --> 24:52.770
<b>There is no Yokohama Prefecture!</b>

24:52.770 --> 24:57.940
<b>Unfortunately, having said that,
I’m out of time to say the next title.</b>

24:55.010 --> 24:59.950
<b>Two Opposing Forces</b>
